WEBVTT

0
00:00:00.009 --> 00:00:03.089
While classical education is a wonderful approach,

1
00:00:03.329 --> 00:00:07.889
implementing it in a public charter school can present a few unique challenges.

2
00:00:08.369 --> 00:00:08.810
First,

3
00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:12.760
the historical order in which classical curricula teach subjects

4
00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:15.800
doesn't always line up with state grade level standards,

5
00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:19.639
requiring careful coordination between parents and teachers.

6
00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:20.690
Second,

7
00:00:20.969 --> 00:00:24.090
many popular classical curricula are non-secular.

8
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:26.579
While families can use these privately,

9
00:00:26.829 --> 00:00:30.899
public charter guidelines mean religious materials cannot currently be used

10
00:00:30.899 --> 00:00:34.130
for official work samples or purchased with charter funds.

11
00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:35.139
Finally,

12
00:00:35.259 --> 00:00:36.840
in the early grammar stage,

13
00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:40.810
much of the learning happens orally through chants and recitations.

14
00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:44.860
This often presents a challenge with collecting a tangible work sample.